1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:05,968
Every show we run starts as a note. This one is Saturday's beach show, in Valencia.

2
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:21,840
Notes is where things get captured — show plans, formulas, supplier quirks. Pinned for the daily stuff, tags for everything else, all in your own database.

3
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:30,573
Starting one is instant. New note, a title, first line — no account, no sync, no spinner.

4
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:44,859
And the editor does real documents, not sticky notes. Headings, task lists, tables, images — markdown, rich text or plain, your call.

5
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:52,208
Need something back? Search hits titles, content and tags in an instant.

6
00:00:56,600 --> 00:01:06,136
But here's the habit that sticks: don't open the module at all. Just tell your agent — rain contingency, tarps, drainage check, a backup date.

7
00:01:08,600 --> 00:01:15,491
Seconds later the note exists — and it comes back as a chip. Click it, and you're there. Created, filed, and linked.

8
00:01:18,600 --> 00:01:26,109
Notes also link outward. Type at — and connect the supplier, the event, the invoice. One tap, and you're in their record.

9
00:01:29,900 --> 00:01:37,665
That's Notes — one module of Micelclaw, your self-hosted AI productivity OS. Next week: Calendar.
